---
/*
 * DocKitty carrier: Header (the fifth carrier, ADR-0044; FR-024, FR-025).
 *
 * REPLACE, never compose: a theme that fills the `dk:site-header` slot gets its
 * component rendered INSTEAD of Starlight's header; with no such slot the stock
 * header renders. This is the one either/or carrier — `Footer` composes around
 * its default because the article footer must survive a brand band, whereas a
 * site has exactly one header.
 *
 * The branch below is deliberately wrapper-free: no host element, no
 * `data-dk-slot` marker, no attribute, and no text or comment node around the
 * expression. Starlight's `PageFrame` already wraps whatever renders here in
 * `<header class="header">`, so anything added would change the header markup of
 * every site that supplies no header (NFR-007: byte-identical to Starlight's
 * stock header, as captured without the carrier by `pnpm fixture:stock-header`,
 * stamped in `src/tests/fixtures/header-theme/stock-header.meta.json`;
 * `header-carrier.test.ts` holds the committed block).
 *
 * Starlight renders this override as `<Header slot="header" />` (re-checked
 * against 0.42.6, #144): no props, no children. The `slot` attribute is
 * consumed by `PageFrame`, and the stock header reads its data from Starlight's
 * virtual modules, so there is nothing to forward. `Astro.props` is still
 * spread onto whichever component renders, so a later Starlight that does pass
 * props reaches the header unchanged.
 *
 * What a `dk:site-header` component gets and gives up (Starlight 0.42.6):
 *
 *  - It renders once, inside Starlight's own `<header class="header">`, which
 *    `PageFrame.astro` owns, with no toolkit wrapper. It must not emit a
 *    `<header>` of its own, and it inherits the positioning, height and padding
 *    of `header.header`.
 *  - The framework keeps the skip link (`Page.astro` renders it before the page
 *    frame) and, on pages with a sidebar, the mobile menu toggle (`PageFrame`
 *    renders it in the sidebar `<nav>`; since 0.42 a `popovertarget` button,
 *    not a custom element). The component supplies neither.
 *  - The theme loses everything the stock header drew, and must supply what it
 *    still wants: the site title and logo, search, the social icons, the theme
 *    select and the language select.
 */
import Default from '@astrojs/starlight/components/Header.astro';
import { slotComponents } from 'virtual:doc-kitty/manifest';

const SiteHeader = slotComponents['dk:site-header'];
---
{SiteHeader ? <SiteHeader {...Astro.props} /> : <Default {...Astro.props} />}
